<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Let's Make a Poster! – Lesson # 3</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;"><i>Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</i></p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 3</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Speaking</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 5th Grade (CEFR: A1.3)</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Following Instructions at School</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> Let's Make a Poster!</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Speaking: Productive: Talk about simple rules and laws.<br>Interactive: Answer questions about their daily routine.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Speaking: Can describe basic classroom rules related to school projects (e.g., "We must clean up after making the poster." "You have to wash your hands after using paint." "We should put away the scissors and glue when we're done.").<br>Can answer and ask follow-up questions to classmates about steps in a class project as part of their routine (e.g., "What do I do after cutting the paper?" "Glue it on the poster." "Where do I put the markers after using them?" "In the supply box.").<br>Can explain safety rules at school when using classroom materials (e.g., "You should use scissors carefully." "Always walk, don't run when carrying sharp objects.").</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 25px;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px; background-color: #f2f2f2; text-align: left; color: #1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px; background-color: #f2f2f2; text-align: left; color: #1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px; background-color: #f2f2f2; text-align: left; color: #1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher shows realia (paper, scissors, glue, crayons) and asks students: "What do we use these for?" "What can we make?" Students respond with single words or short phrases. Teacher guides to "We can make a poster!" or "We can make a card!" Teacher asks: "What do we call this?" while pointing to scissors, "scissors" (/s/ sound emphasized). "And this?" pointing to paper, "paper" (/p/ sound emphasized). Students repeat words in chorus.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher demonstrates a simple action, e.g., cutting a piece of paper. "First, I take the paper. Next, I cut the paper." The teacher models the pronunciation of /p/ in "paper" and /s/ in "scissors." The teacher also models "classroom" and claps out syllables "class-room" to highlight two syllables.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Do we cut with glue or with scissors?" (Expected: "With scissors!")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Can we run with scissors?" (Expected: "No!")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Is 'classroom' one word or two parts?" (Expected: "Two parts!")</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Following Instructions at School".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> Illustrated sequence of instructions for making a simple paper mask. The instructions are presented on large flashcards or projected on the board, showing visual steps for "cut," "fold," "paste," "draw." The instructions use imperative forms and sequencing words: "First, cut the paper. Next, fold the paper. Then, paste the eyes. Finally, draw a mouth."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> The student follows and gives simple instructions for a school project.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Listen and Point:</b> Teacher reads an instruction (e.g., "Paste the eyes."), students point to the correct picture.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Order the Pictures:</b> Teacher scrambles the pictures/flashcards of the mask-making steps. Students work in pairs to verbally put them in the correct order, saying: "First is...", "Next is..."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False:</b> Teacher makes a statement about the steps (e.g., "First, we draw the mouth.") and students say "True" or "False."</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Speaking. Using target grammar and vocabulary.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students practice plural imperatives ("Let's make a poster!"), sequencing words ("first, next, then, finally"), future tense ("I will make a mask," "I am going to make a mask"), and vocabulary (paper, scissors, glue, pencil, poster, cut, fold, paste, draw).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Imperative Chain Drill:</b> Teacher starts a chain: "First, cut the paper." The next student repeats and adds an instruction: "First, cut the paper. Next, fold it." The third student continues. This builds a sequence of instructions, focusing on correct sequencing words and target verbs.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Picture-Cued Instructions (Pair Work):</b> Students work in pairs. Each pair receives a set of picture cards depicting steps for a simple craft (e.g., making a paper boat or a simple drawing). One student describes the steps using sequencing words and imperatives ("First, take the big paper. Next, fold it.") while the partner points to the correct picture. Then they switch roles. Teacher reminds them to use words like "big," "small," "colorful."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Future Plans & Clarification Role-Play:</b> Students are in pairs. One student says what they *will* do for an upcoming classroom project using future tense (e.g., "I will draw a colorful flower on my poster."). The partner asks for clarification or follow-up: "What do you need to do next?" or "Where will you put the flower?" The first student responds (e.g., "Next, I will paste it on the poster." or "I will put it on the top."). Encourage the use of prepositions like "on," "in."</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Following Instructions at School".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Collaborative Poster Creation (Group Role-Play).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Description:</b> Students work in small groups (3-4 students) to collaboratively create a "Welcome to our Classroom" poster using various art materials (big paper, crayons, markers, scissors, glue, small pieces of cardboard/fabric). Each group is given a set of materials and a general theme. Students must communicate actively to decide what to do and how to do it. They will give each other instructions, ask for clarification, and state their intentions. Teacher encourages the use of "Let's..." for collaboration, imperatives for instructions, sequencing words, future tense to describe what they are going to do, and safety rules.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Example Dialogue Snippets:</b></p>
                <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Let's make a big sun here!"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"First, cut the blue paper for the sky."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What do I need to do next after cutting?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Paste it on the top of the poster."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"You should use scissors carefully. Always walk, don't run."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"I am going to draw a happy face on this mask."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"We must clean up after making the poster."</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">The teacher circulates, observing and providing support as needed, ensuring all students are speaking and interacting.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy and student reflection.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher Observation Checklist during the "Collaborative Poster Creation" activity. The teacher will observe each student's participation in group discussions, their ability to give and follow instructions, ask for clarification, and use target language.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students actively participate in their groups to create the poster, communicating effectively with classmates by giving instructions, asking questions, and stating intentions related to the project and classroom rules.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b></p>
                <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Intelligible pronunciation of /p/ in "poster" and /s/ in "scissors."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Use of target vocabulary (nouns: paper, scissors, glue; verbs: cut, paste, draw).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clear use of imperatives ("Cut the paper," "Let's draw!").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Use of sequencing words ("First, next, then, finally").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Asking for clarification ("What do I need to do next?").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Communicating future intentions ("I will make a mask.").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Collaborating with classmates (e.g., using "Let's...").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Explaining safety rules (e.g., "You should use scissors carefully.").</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete a short exit ticket before leaving the classroom.</p>
                <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Today, I can give instructions about..."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One thing I will make for a project is..."</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Review of learning and preparation for the next lesson.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Reflection:</b></p>
                <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How well did I give instructions to my classmates today?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of working in a group was easy for me? What was difficult?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher Reflection:</b></p>
                <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in this speaking lesson? (e.g., Most students actively used imperatives and sequencing words during the poster activity. Group collaboration was good.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or additional scaffolds are needed for the next lesson? (e.g., Some students struggled with asking for clarification naturally; need more targeted practice. Ensure more materials for next time to keep all students engaged.)</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> "Great job speaking and making our posters today! In our next lesson (Lesson 4), we will take the instructions we used and write them down to create a short guide on how to make a poster. We will practice writing sentences with our new vocabulary and sequencing words."</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>